---
source: tests/cli_help.rs
expression: stdout
---
Create a sanitized, reproducible review bundle from a Git repository

Usage: Rustrepo-sanitizer sanitize [OPTIONS] [REPOSITORY]

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

Repository / input:
      --include-untracked  Also include files Git does not track yet, subject to safety filters.
  [REPOSITORY]             Git repository to sanitize; defaults to the current directory. [default:
                           .]

Output:
  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Destination archive path; leave blank to derive a filename in the repository root.
      --timestamp-name <TIMESTAMP_NAME>
          Add a timestamp and commit id to the automatic output filename. [default: true] [possible
          values: true, false]

Archive / compression:
      --archive <ARCHIVE>          Archive container: none (JSONL stream), tar, zip, or 7z.
                                   [default: tar] [alias: --format] [possible values: none, tar,
                                   zip, 7z]
      --compression <COMPRESSION>  Compression codec; only codecs valid for the chosen archive are
                                   accepted. [default: zstd] [possible values: none, gzip, zstd,
                                   lz4, lzip, lzma, lzo, lrzip, xz, zlib, brotli, snappy, bzip2]

Include / exclude:
      --include <INCLUDE>              Git-style glob of paths to include; repeat for more patterns.
      --exclude <EXCLUDE>              Git-style glob of paths to exclude; repeat for more patterns.
      --max-file-size <MAX_FILE_SIZE>  Maximum file size; accepts plain bytes or KiB/MiB/GiB.
                                       [default: 10MiB]

Redaction / sanitization:
      --redact <REDACT>  Replace high-confidence secret values with redaction markers. [default:
                         true] [possible values: true, false]
      --no-redact        Disable redaction of detected secret values.
      --fail-on-secret   Stop with an error instead of producing output when a secret is found.

Reports / metadata:
      --report <REPORT>  Report format: markdown, json, or none. [default: markdown] [possible
                         values: markdown, json, none]
      --dry-run          Scan and report results without writing an archive.

Security / password:
      --password-file <PASSWORD_FILE>
          Read the ZIP AES password from this file.
      --password-stdin
          Read the ZIP AES password from standard input.
      --password-min-length <PASSWORD_MIN_LENGTH>
          Minimum number of characters required in a password. [default: 8]
      --password-require-uppercase <PASSWORD_REQUIRE_UPPERCASE>
          Require at least one uppercase letter in the password. [default: true] [possible values:
          true, false]
      --password-require-lowercase <PASSWORD_REQUIRE_LOWERCASE>
          Require at least one lowercase letter in the password. [default: true] [possible values:
          true, false]
      --password-require-number <PASSWORD_REQUIRE_NUMBER>
          Require at least one digit in the password. [default: true] [possible values: true, false]
      --password-require-special <PASSWORD_REQUIRE_SPECIAL>
          Require at least one special character in the password. [default: true] [possible values:
          true, false]

Advanced:
  -v, --verbose  Print per-file progress details.
  -q, --quiet    Suppress the final summary line.
